OTHER WORK THIS PROJECT RESTS ON

Nothing below is vendored here. It is listed because a dependency file records
what to install, not who did the work, and "we borrowed nothing" is a claim
worth being able to check.

METHOD, CITED WHERE IT IS USED

  Reciprocal rank fusion -- Cormack, Clarke and Buettcher, "Reciprocal Rank
  Fusion outperforms Condorcet and individual Rank Learning Methods", SIGIR
  2009. Implemented in `morpho_homegraph/fusion.py`; k = 60 is their reported
  value, kept rather than tuned.

MODEL, FETCHED AT RUN TIME AND NOT REDISTRIBUTED

  `paraphrase-multilingual-MiniLM-L12-v2` -- a sentence-transformers model
  (Reimers and Gurevych, UKP Lab), used through the `Xenova/` conversion for
  transformers.js. Named in `morpho_homegraph/embed.py`.

LIBRARIES

  `@xenova/transformers` (npm) -- the embedding worker's runtime.
  `numpy` -- cosine over float32 blobs in `embed.py`.
  Python's standard library does the rest, SQLite and FTS5 included.

CODE FROM THE PREDECESSOR PROJECT

  Two test-harness files and one analysis tool were copied from `homegraph`,
  an earlier project by the same author, and each says so in its own docstring
  with the source commit:

    tests/mutate.py                 the one mutation driver
    tests/report.py                 the `check()` used by every gate file
    tests/condition_coverage.py     compound-condition detector, carries
                                    SOURCE_SHA256 and re-hashes its source

  `morpho_homegraph/watch.py` is the same predecessor's inotify layer at commit
  2ce3462d, with the parts that assumed no long-running service left behind.

  `morpho_homegraph/lock.py` is explicitly NOT borrowed. The predecessor's
  version had a window where two writers could both hold the guard, and the
  file says so where a reader will meet it.
